The @ai-ctx directory has detailed documentation of key concepts and intended practices for the project.

### ai-ctx/*.md

Refernce documentation for difficult concepts and connections to other repositories.
This is the refined hub that builds out the custom knowledge base we'll use for effective prompting.

### ai-ctx/rules

Rules are meant to be used by various LLM tools, not cursor. Rules are also stored in `ai-ctx`.
For example, cursor sees them via symlinks inside of .cursor/rules as `*.mdc` files. On the other hand, 
`claude` won't look at the `.cursor` directory, so it's better to keep things in a directory that's visible 
by default.